---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import NarrativeImage from '../components/NarrativeImage.astro';
import Invitation from '../components/Invitation.astro';
import Process from '../components/Process.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Fractional AI support & delivery"
  description="Experienced AI support alongside your CTO or internal advocate. Assess opportunities, make the case to leadership, build agents and develop ownership in your team."
  service="Fractional AI consultancy and delivery"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap interior-hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow red">Fractional AI support & delivery</p><h1>
          Move AI forward.<br />With experienced<br />help alongside you.
        </h1><p class="lead">
          You have opportunities to explore and a business to keep running. Get ongoing help
          deciding what is worth doing, making the case, and getting it built.
        </p><a class="button" href="/enquire/?need=business"
          >Discuss fractional support <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        ><p class="availability">Contract and fractional engagements. Remote preferred.</p>
      </div><div class="small-paper" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>Worth doing?</span><span>Let’s work<br />that out.</span><b>↗</b>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="wrap reading-layout section editorial-layout">
    <nav class="contents" aria-label="On this page">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <a href="#making-the-case">Working alongside your team</a>
      <a href="#recent-experience">Recent experience</a>
      <a href="#what-we-can-do">What we can work on</a>
      <a href="#how-we-start">How we start</a>
      <a href="#questions">Practical questions</a>
      <a class="text-link" href="/enquire/?need=business">Discuss your brief ↗</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="prose editorial-prose">
      <section id="making-the-case">
        <h2>Build a business case alongside your CTO.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Experienced support for the person moving AI forward inside your business.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may have a CTO or an internal advocate with opportunities to explore and limited time
          to pursue them. I work alongside them, bringing technical backing and practical delivery
          so leadership has something concrete to assess.
        </p>
        <p>
          The starting point is useful work: a new customer channel, better access to business
          knowledge, or a workflow your team doesn’t have capacity to run. We consider the value,
          effort and uncertainties together.
        </p>
        <NarrativeImage
          name="working-together"
          alt="Documents connect through simple modules to an organised briefing."
          caption="Turn scattered information into something useful."
        />
      </section>
      <section id="recent-experience" class="evidence-chapter">
        <h2>Recent work, from question to outcome.</h2>
        <p>Two examples of how an engagement can develop. Client names are omitted.</p>
        <article id="travel" class="case-account">
          <h3>Travel: finding a better direction.</h3>
          <dl class="case-facts">
            <div>
              <dt>Situation</dt><dd>
                A travel business wanted to explore an AI customer-discovery channel.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Work</dt><dd>
                A prototype tested the opportunity. The findings helped redirect investment towards
                a customer-facing agent on the company’s own website.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Outcome</dt><dd>
                A better-informed direction, with the development team supported and trained to take
                ownership of the implementation.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </article>
        <article id="ev-project" class="case-account">
          <h3>EV sector: supporting an internal AI specialist.</h3>
          <dl class="case-facts">
            <div>
              <dt>Situation</dt><dd>
                The business was exploring AI applications across management teams.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Work</dt><dd>
                Practical experiments alongside training for an in-house AI specialist.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Outcome</dt><dd>
                Support for someone inside the business to develop the knowledge and confidence to
                carry the work forward.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </article>
      </section>
      <section id="what-we-can-do">
        <h2>Advice, engineering and team support.</h2>
        <p>Your needs determine the mix. An engagement can develop across these areas.</p>
        <div class="service-rows">
          <article>
            <div>
              <h3>Opportunity &amp; business case</h3><p class="row-answer">
                A next step leadership can assess.
              </p>
            </div><p>
              Identify useful applications, assess feasibility and make the trade-offs clear. A
              focused experiment can test an assumption before a larger commitment.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <div>
              <h3>Agents, workflows &amp; integrations</h3><p class="row-answer">
                Useful tools connected to your work.
              </p>
            </div><p>
              Build internal or customer-facing agents and connect shared context. That can include
              MCP servers, skill libraries, CRM extensions, dashboards and visible automations. We
              choose between existing products and a custom build according to the need.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <div>
              <h3>Team adoption &amp; ownership</h3><p class="row-answer">
                People who can keep it working.
              </p>
            </div><p>
              Help your team use the tools confidently, whether through a familiar interface or by
              directing an agent. Support can include an in-house specialist looking after shared
              skills, permissions, context and conventions.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="how-we-start" class="engagement-start">
        <Process />
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="narrative-panorama" aria-hidden="true">
    <img
      src="/images/narrative/workbench-action-panorama-1800.webp"
      srcset="/images/narrative/workbench-action-panorama-900.webp 900w, /images/narrative/workbench-action-panorama-1800.webp 1800w"
      sizes="(max-width: 599px) calc(100vw - 40px), (max-width: 1500px) 80vw, 1200px"
      width="1800"
      height="600"
      alt=""
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
    />
  </div>
  <section class="faq-section section" id="questions">
    <div class="wrap reading-layout">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The practical bits</p><h2>Scope, fees &amp;<br />working together.</h2>
      </div><div class="faqs">
        <article class="faq-answer">
          <h3>Can you work alongside our CTO?</h3><p>
            Yes. Support can sit alongside your existing technical leadership. We agree who makes
            decisions, who does the work, and who owns it internally.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-answer">
          <h3>Can we start with a defined project?</h3><p>
            Yes. A specific opportunity can be a starting point. We can also discuss ongoing support
            if you need help across several decisions or pieces of work.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-answer">
          <h3>How are scope and fees agreed?</h3><p>
            We discuss the outcome, the work involved, and the level of ongoing support before
            agreeing an engagement. You can send an initial brief even if the scope is still taking
            shape.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-answer">
          <h3>Do you work remotely?</h3><p>
            Yes. Remote engagements are preferred. In-person work in Bristol can be arranged.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-answer">
          <h3>Are you available for permanent roles?</h3><p>
            I take on fractional and contract work. If you are a recruiter with an opportunity that
            fits, send the brief and the expected working arrangement.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Invitation title="What are you trying to move forward?" />
</Layout>
